 Agent Builder: Connecting Enterprise Data to the AI Ecosystem</title><link>https://chatforest.com/guides/domo-mcp-server-enterprise-ai-agents/</link><guid>https://chatforest.com/guides/domo-mcp-server-enterprise-ai-agents/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 07 Apr 2026 14:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>Domo launched an MCP Server and AI Agent Builder at Domopalooza 2026 — connecting enterprise datasets, workflows, and interactive dashboards to external AI platforms like Claude, Gemini, and ChatGPT.</description></item><item><title>Conway: Anthropic's Always-On Agent Platform Turns Claude Into a Persistent Digital Worker</title><link>https://chatforest.com/guides/anthropic-conway-always-on-agent-platform/</link><guid>https://chatforest.com/guides/anthropic-conway-always-on-agent-platform/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 07 Apr 2026 14:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>Anthropic is testing Conway, a persistent always-on agent platform that transforms Claude from a reactive chatbot into a 24/7 autonomous worker. Conway features webhook-triggered activation, a .cnw.zip extension ecosystem, Chrome browser integration, and a standalone UI — positioning it as Anthropic's most ambitious agent infrastructure play yet.</description></item><item><title>Uber's MCP Gateway: How 84% of Engineers Went Agentic and What It Took to Get There</title><link>https://chatforest.com/guides/uber-mcp-gateway-agentic-engineering/</link><guid>https://chatforest.com/guides/uber-mcp-gateway-agentic-engineering/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 07 Apr 2026 10:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>Uber built a centralized MCP Gateway that turns any internal endpoint into an MCP server, paired with a no-code Agent Builder and discovery registry. With 84% developer adoption, 65-72% AI-generated code, and 11% of PRs opened by agents, this is one of the largest enterprise MCP deployments documented.</description></item><item><title>Holo3: How a 10B-Parameter Open Model Beat GPT-5.4 and Opus 4.6 at Controlling Desktops</title><link>https://chatforest.com/guides/holo3-desktop-agent-osworld-record/</link><guid>https://chatforest.com/guides/holo3-desktop-agent-osworld-record/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 07 Apr 2026 01:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>H Company's Holo3 sets a new state of the art on OSWorld-Verified at 78.85% — beating proprietary models with a fraction of the active parameters. The open-source 3B-active variant scores 77.8% under Apache 2.0. Here's the architecture, training pipeline, and what it means for desktop automation.</description></item><item><title>Red Hat's MCP Ecosystem for RHEL: From Log Analysis to Vulnerability Remediation</title><link>https://chatforest.com/guides/red-hat-mcp-server-rhel-lightspeed/</link><guid>https://chatforest.com/guides/red-hat-mcp-server-rhel-lightspeed/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Apr 2026 23:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>Red Hat shipped MCP servers for RHEL troubleshooting, vulnerability management, image building, and infrastructure health — all read-only by default, containerized via Podman, and integrated with Red Hat Insights. Here's how the ecosystem works.</description></item><item><title>Fingerprint's MCP Server: How Device Intelligence Is Bringing AI to Fraud Prevention</title><link>https://chatforest.com/guides/fingerprint-mcp-server-fraud-device-intelligence/</link><guid>https://chatforest.com/guides/fingerprint-mcp-server-fraud-device-intelligence/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Apr 2026 23:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>Fingerprint launched the first open-source MCP server for fraud prevention — connecting AI assistants to device intelligence, Smart Signals, and workspace management. Here's how it works, what it exposes, and why it matters for fintech and e-commerce teams.</description></item><item><title>Claude Wrote a FreeBSD Kernel Exploit in Four Hours — What AI-Powered Vulnerability Research Means for Security</title><link>https://chatforest.com/guides/claude-freebsd-exploit-ai-vulnerability-research/</link><guid>https://chatforest.com/guides/claude-freebsd-exploit-ai-vulnerability-research/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Apr 2026 23:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>Anthropic's Frontier Red Team had Claude Opus 4.6 autonomously develop two working remote root exploits for FreeBSD kernel flaw CVE-2026-4747 in roughly four hours. The same research pipeline has found 500+ high-severity vulnerabilities across major open-source projects. Here's what happened, how it works, and why it changes the security calculus for every team running production infrastructure.</description></item><item><title>Equinix's Distributed AI Hub: How Fabric Intelligence and MCP Are Automating Network Infrastructure</title><link>https://chatforest.com/guides/equinix-distributed-ai-hub-mcp-infrastructure/</link><guid>https://chatforest.com/guides/equinix-distributed-ai-hub-mcp-infrastructure/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Apr 2026 22:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>Equinix built a vendor-neutral AI hub across 280 data centers, with an MCP server exposing 40+ network automation tools and a Palo Alto Networks security partnership. Here's how it works.</description></item><item><title>Salesforce's Slack AI Overhaul: MCP Client, 30 New Features, and the Agentforce Connection</title><link>https://chatforest.com/guides/salesforce-slack-mcp-ai-platform/</link><guid>https://chatforest.com/guides/salesforce-slack-mcp-ai-platform/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Apr 2026 21:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>Salesforce is turning Slackbot into an MCP client that connects to 6,000+ enterprise apps via Agentforce. Here's the architecture, the 30 new AI features, and what it means for the MCP ecosystem.</description></item><item><title>A2A Protocol v1.0: What It Means for Agent-to-Agent Communication in Production</title><link>https://chatforest.com/guides/a2a-protocol-v1-production-ready/</link><guid>https://chatforest.com/guides/a2a-protocol-v1-production-ready/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Apr 2026 21:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>A2A Protocol hit v1.0 on March 12, 2026. gRPC, signed Agent Cards, 5-language SDKs, AWS/Azure/Google Cloud support, 150+ orgs. What changed from v0.3 and what's next.</description></item><item><title>MCP Apps: How Anthropic and OpenAI Brought Interactive UIs to AI Chat</title><link>https://chatforest.com/guides/mcp-apps-interactive-ui-extension/</link><guid>https://chatforest.com/guides/mcp-apps-interactive-ui-extension/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Apr 2026 20:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>MCP's first official extension lets servers render interactive dashboards, forms, and visualizations inside AI conversations. Ten launch partners shipped on day one. Here's how it works, who's using it, and what it means for MCP's future.</description></item><item><title>Docker's MCP Platform: How the Gateway, Catalog, and Toolkit Are Securing AI Agents at Scale</title><link>https://chatforest.com/guides/docker-mcp-platform-gateway-security/</link><guid>https://chatforest.com/guides/docker-mcp-platform-gateway-security/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Apr 2026 20:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>Docker built a three-layer MCP platform — a 300+ server Catalog, a Desktop Toolkit, and an open-source Gateway with interceptors and secret blocking. Here's how it works and why it matters for production MCP security.</description></item><item><title>MCP's Growing Pains: Context Bloat, Security Gaps, and the Companies Walking Away</title><link>https://chatforest.com/guides/mcp-growing-pains-2026/</link><guid>https://chatforest.com/guides/mcp-growing-pains-2026/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Apr 2026 18:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>MCP won the standard war but production reality is catching up — 72% context window waste, 30+ CVEs in 60 days, and companies like Perplexity abandoning it internally. Here's what's breaking, who's leaving, and whether the 2026 roadmap fixes it.</description></item><item><title>Duolingo's Agentic AI Platform: 180+ MCP Tools, No-Code Workflows, and an Enterprise Slackbot</title><link>https://chatforest.com/guide